  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-86474\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>A mathematical statement is a sentence or mathematical expression that is either true or false. </p>\n<p>Of the given sentences, the only sentence that is either true or false is \"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"75\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> is a positive number.\" (This sentence is true.)</p>\n<p>All the other sentences are neither true nor false.</p>\n<div class=\"studentAnswerHeader\">Your Answer:</div><div class=\"studentAnswer\">The set of the odd numbers.</div></div>",
